WEBVTT

00:01.331 --> 00:14.438
Broken tracking usually shows up weeks later. Analytics Health checks every PMW site every morning, so you know the next day.

00:14.646 --> 00:20.557
Up top is the whole picture: how many sites are healthy, how many need a look, and how many are critical.

00:20.745 --> 00:24.517
Switch between all sites, Elite and PMI with one click.

00:24.694 --> 00:30.890
Search for a site, or filter by problem: tracking, analytics, data quality or conversions.

00:31.078 --> 00:37.750
One row per site, worst first. A red mark shows exactly which check failed.

00:39.177 --> 00:43.828
Open a site, and you get a plain verdict: what's wrong, and how serious it is.

00:44.012 --> 00:48.940
Each issue shows the numbers before and after, so it's easy to explain.

00:49.127 --> 00:57.319
What the site should track: its GA4 property, tag manager, and expected events and conversions.

00:57.510 --> 01:02.211
Up to 90 days of history, so you can see exactly when a drop started.

01:03.645 --> 01:08.464
Monthly page views adds up traffic across every monitored site, month by month.

01:08.643 --> 01:14.451
Twelve months at a glance, and a spreadsheet download for reports.

01:15.859 --> 01:22.643
Every GA4 property our logins can see, each counted once.

01:22.825 --> 01:28.646
Switches leave out duplicates, roll-ups and internal sites, so the total stays honest.

01:28.798 --> 01:36.836
New critical problems also land in Slack every morning. Broken tracking gets caught the next day, not at month end.
